   "source": [
    "# 📊 StockMarket AI - Baseline Modeling\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Establish baseline performance for predicting RELIANCE.NS stock movements using technical indicators\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    ## 🎯 What We'll Accomplish\n",
    "- Load your engineered features from `reliance_ml_ready.csv`\n",
    "- Establish baseline models (Logistic Regression & Random Forest)\n",
    "- Analyze feature importance\n",
    "- Save trained models and preprocessing objects\n",
    "- Create example prediction function\n",
    "\n",
    > **Note:** This notebook assumes you've completed Phase 1-4 (data collection & feature engineering)\n",
    "  and have `data/processed/reliance_ml_ready.csv` available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣ Import Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start by importing all necessary libraries for data analysis and machine learning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "# 02_model_baseline.ipynb - Baseline Model for StockMarket AI\n",
    "# ============================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. IMPORT LIBRARIES\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix, roc_auc_score, f1_score\n",
    "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set plotting style\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📊 StockMarket AI - Baseline Modeling Phase\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2️⃣ Load Your Processed Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll load the ML-ready dataset you created during feature engineering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2. LOAD YOUR PROCESSED DATA\n",
    "print(\"\\n1️⃣ Loading processed data...\")\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('data/processed/reliance_ml_ready.csv', index_col='Date', parse_dates=True)\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Loaded: {df.shape[0]} rows, {df.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
    "print(f\"📅 Date range: {df.index.min().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} to {df.index.max().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display first few rows\n",
    "display(df.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3️⃣ Explore Target Variable\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine our target variable - what are we trying to predict?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 3. EXPLORE TARGET VARIABLE\n",
    "print(\"\\n2️⃣ Analyzing target variable...\")\n",
    "target_balance = df['Target'].mean()\n",
    "print(f\"🎯 Target distribution:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - Class 0 (Down/No move): {(1-target_balance)*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - Class 1 (Up): {target_balance*100:.1f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check for class imbalance\n",
    "if abs(target_balance - 0.5) > 0.15:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️  Significant class imbalance detected - will use SMOTE\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"✅ Reasonable class balance\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot target distribution\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "df['Target'].value_counts().plot(kind='bar', color=['skyblue', 'lightcoral'])\n",
    "plt.title('Target Variable Distribution', fontsize=16, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Target Class (0=Down, 1=Up)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Count', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n",
    "# Add value labels on bars\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(df['Target'].value_counts().values):\n",
    "    plt.text(i, v + max(df['Target'].value_counts())*0.01, str(v), ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4️⃣ Prepare Features and Target\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we'll separate our features (X) from our target variable (y) and handle any missing values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 4. PREPARE FEATURES AND TARGET\n",
    "print(\"\\n3️⃣ Preparing features and target...\")\n",
    "feature_cols = [col for col in df.columns if col != 'Target']\n",
    "X = df[feature_cols]\n",
    "y = df['Target']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Number of features: {len(feature_cols)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"📋 Feature names: {feature_cols}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Handle NaN values from rolling indicators (forward fill then backward fill)\n",
    "missing_before = X.isnull().sum().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"🔧 Handling {missing_before} missing values...\")\n",
    "X = X.fillna(method='ffill').fillna(method='bfill')\n",
    "missing_after = X.isnull().sum().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Missing values after processing: {missing_after}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show data info\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📈 Data info after cleaning:\")\n",
    "print(X.info())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5️⃣ Create Temporal Train/Test Split\n",
    "\n",
    "⚠️ **CRITICAL for financial data:** We must maintain temporal order to avoid data leakage!\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use the first 80% of data for training and the most recent 20% for testing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 5. TEMPORAL TRAIN/TEST SPLIT (CRITICAL FOR TIME SERIES!)\n",
    "print(\"\\n4️⃣ Creating temporal train/test split...\")\n",
    "split_idx = int(len(df) * 0.8)  # 80% for training, 20% for testing\n",
    "X_train, X_test = X.iloc[:split_idx], X.iloc[split_idx:]\n",
    "y_train, y_test = y.iloc[:split_idx], y.iloc[split_idx:]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"📈 Training set:  {X_train.shape[0]} samples ({X_train.index.min().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} to {X_train.index.max().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')})\")\n",
    "print(f\"📉 Test set:      {X_test.shape[0]} samples ({X_test.index.min().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')} to {X_test.index.max().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')})\")\n",
    "print(f\"🔒 Split maintains temporal order - essential for financial data!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify no overlap in time\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✅ Temporal separation verified: train ends {X_train.index.max()}, test starts {X_test.index.min()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6️⃣ Feature Scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "Most machine learning algorithms perform better when features are on a similar scale.\n",
    "We'll use StandardScaler to standardize features (mean=0, std=1)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 6. FEATURE SCALING\n",
    "print(\"\\n5️⃣ Scaling features...\")\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "print(\"✅ Features standardized (mean=0, std=1)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify scaling worked\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Scaling verification:\")\n",
    print(f\"   Training set - Mean: {X_train_scaled.mean():.6f}, Std: {X_train_scaled.std():.6f}\")\n",
    print(f\"   Test set - Mean: {X_test_scaled.mean():.6f}, Std: {X_test_scaled.std():.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7️⃣ Handle Class Imbalance (If Needed)\n",
    "\n",
    "If our classes are significantly imbalanced, we'll use SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique)\n",
    "to create synthetic samples of the minority class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 7. HANDLE CLASS IMBALANCE IF NEEDED\n",
    "print(\"\\n6️⃣ Checking for class imbalance...\")\n",
    "train_balance = y_train.mean()\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Training set target balance: {train_balance:.3f} ({train_balance*100:.1f}% Class 1)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if abs(train_balance - 0.5) > 0.1:  # >10% imbalance\n",
    "    print(\"⚖️  Applying SMOTE to balance training data...\")\n",
    "    smote = SMOTE(random_state=42)\n",
    "    X_train_balanced, y_train_balanced = smote.fit_resample(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "    print(f\"📊 Balanced training set: {X_train_balanced.shape[0]} samples\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Original: {X_train_scaled.shape[0]} samples\")\n",
    "    print(f"   Synthetic samples added: {X_train_balanced.shape[0] - X_train_scaled.shape[0]}"\n",
    ")",
    "else:\n",
    "    X_train_balanced, y_train_balanced = X_train_scaled, y_train\n",
    "    print(\"✅ No significant imbalance - using original training data\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8️⃣ Baseline Model 1: Logistic Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start with a simple, interpretable baseline model - Logistic Regression.\n",
    "This gives us a good benchmark to compare more complex models against."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 8. BASELINE MODEL 1: LOGISTIC REGRESSION\n",
    "print(\"\\n7️⃣ Training Logistic Regression (baseline)...\")\n",
    "lr = LogisticRegression(\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    max_iter=1000,\n",
    "    class_weight='balanced' if abs(y_train.mean() - 0.5) > 0.1 else None,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "lr.fit(X_train_balanced, y_train_balanced)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "y_pred_lr = lr.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "y_pred_proba_lr = lr.predict_proba(X_test_scaled)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Metrics\n",
    "lr_f1 = f1_score(y_test, y_pred_lr)\n",
    "lr_auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_pred_proba_lr)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"📈 Logistic Regression Results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - F1-Score: {lr_f1:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - ROC AUC:  {lr_auc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Detailed classification report\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Detailed Classification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_lr, target_names=['Down (0)', 'Up (1)']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9️⃣ Baseline Model 2: Random Forest\n",
    "\n",
    "Random Forest is an ensemble method that often performs well on financial data\n",
    "due to its ability to capture non-linear relationships and handle feature interactions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 9. BASELINE MODEL 2: RANDOM FOREST\n",
    "print(\"\\n8️⃣ Training Random Forest...\")\n",
    "rf = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=100,\n",
    "    max_depth=10,\n",
    "    min_samples_split=5,\n",
    "    min_samples_leaf=2,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    class_weight='balanced' if abs(y_train.mean() - 0.5) > 0.1 else None,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "rf.fit(X_train_balanced, y_train_balanced)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "y_pred_rf = rf.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "y_pred_proba_rf = rf.predict_proba(X_test_scaled)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Metrics\n",
    "rf_f1 = f1_score(y_test, y_pred_rf)\n",
    "rf_auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_pred_proba_rf)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"🌲 Random Forest Results:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - F1-Score: {rf_f1:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   - ROC AUC:  {rf_auc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Detailed classification report\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📋 Detailed Classification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_rf, target_names=['Down (0)', 'Up (1)']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔟 Model Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's compare our two baseline models side-by-side."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 10. MODEL COMPARISON\n",
    "print(\"\\n9️⃣ Model Comparison...\")\n",
    "results_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'Model': ['Logistic Regression', 'Random Forest'],\n",
    "    'F1-Score': [lr_f1, rf_f1],\n",
    "    'ROC AUC': [lr_auc, rf_auc]\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(results_df.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Determine best model\n",
    "best_model_name = results_df.loc[results_df['F1-Score'].idxmax(), 'Model']\n",
    "print(f\"\\n🏆 Best model based on F1-Score: {best_model_name}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visual comparison\n",
    "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# F1-Score comparison\n",
    "ax1.bar(results_df['Model'], results_df['F1-Score'], color=['skyblue', 'lightgreen'])\n",
    "ax1.set_title('F1-Score Comparison', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylabel('F1-Score')\n",
    "ax1.set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(results_df['F1-Score']):\n",
    "    ax1.text(i, v + 0.02, f'{v:.3f}', ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ROC AUC comparison\n",
    "ax2.bar(results_df['Model'], results_df['ROC AUC'], color=['skyblue', 'lightgreen'])\n",
    "ax2.set_title('ROC AUC Comparison', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylabel('ROC AUC')\n",
    "ax2.set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(results_df['ROC AUC']):\n",
    "    ax2.text(i, v + 0.02, f'{v:.3f}', ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣1️⃣ Feature Importance (From Random Forest)\n",
    "\n",
    "One of the advantages of Random Forest is that it provides feature importance scores,\n",
    "helping us understand which technical indicators are most predictive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 11. FEATURE IMPORTANCE (FROM RANDOM FOREST)\n",
    "print(\"\\n🔟 Analyzing feature importance...\")\n",
    "feature_importance = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'feature': feature_cols,\n",
    "    'importance': rf.feature_importances_\n",
    "}).sort_values('importance', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTop 15 Most Important Features:\")\n",
    "print(feature_importance.head(15).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot feature importance\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=feature_importance.head(15), x='importance', y='feature', palette='viridis')\n",
    "plt.title('Top 15 Feature Importances (Random Forest)', fontsize=16, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Importance Score', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Features', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show all feature importances\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Complete feature importance ranking:\")\n",
    "for idx, row in feature_importance.iterrows():\n",
    "    print(f\"   {row['feature']:<20}: {row['importance']:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣2️⃣ Confusion Matrix for Best Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine where our best model makes predictions correctly and where it errs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 12. CONFUSION MATRIX FOR BEST MODEL\n",
    "print(\"\\n1️⃣1️⃣ Generating confusion matrix...\")\n",
    "best_model = rf if best_model_name == 'Random Forest' else lr\n",
    "y_pred_best = best_model.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_best)\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues',\n",
    "            xticklabels=['Predicted Down (0)', 'Predicted Up (1)'],\n",
    "            yticklabels=['Actual Down (0)', 'Actual Up (1)'])\n",
    "plt.title(f'Confusion Matrix - {best_model_name}', fontsize=16, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Actual Label', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Predicted Label', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate additional metrics from confusion matrix\n",
    "tn, fp, fn, tp = cm.ravel()\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Confusion Matrix Details:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   True Negatives (TN):  {tn}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   False Positives (FP): {fp}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   False Negatives (FN): {fn}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   True Positives (TP):  {tp}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📈 Derived Metrics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Accuracy:  {(tn+tp)/(tn+fp+fn+tp):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Precision: {tp/(tp+fp) if (tp+fp) > 0 else 0:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Recall:    {tp/(tp+fn) if (tp+fn) > 0 else 0:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Specificity:{tn/(tn+fp) if (tn+fp) > 0 else 0:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣3️⃣ Save Model and Preprocessing Objects\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we'll save our trained model, scaler, and feature list so we can use them later\n",
    "for making predictions on new data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 13. SAVE YOUR MODEL AND PREPROCESSING OBJECTS\n",
    "print(\"\\n1️⃣2️⃣ Saving model and preprocessing objects...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create models directory\n",
    "os.makedirs('models', exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the best model\n",
    "model_filename = 'stock_rf_model.pkl' if best_model_name == 'Random Forest' else 'stock_lr_model.pkl'\n",
    "joblib.dump(best_model, f'models/{model_filename}')\n",
    "joblib.dump(scaler, 'models/feature_scaler.pkl')\n",
    "joblib.dump(feature_cols, 'models/feature_columns.pkl')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"💾 Saved model: models/{model_filename}\")\n",
    "print(\"💾 Saved scaler: models/feature_scaler.pkl\")\n",
    "print(\"💾 Saved feature list: models/feature_columns.pkl\")\n",
    "print(\"✅ Modeling baseline complete!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify files were saved\n",
    "print(f\"\\n🔍 Verifying saved files:\")\n",
    "import os\n",
    "for file in ['models/stock_rf_model.pkl', 'models/stock_lr_model.pkl', 'models/feature_scaler.pkl', 'models/feature_columns.pkl']:\n",
    "    if os.path.exists(file):\n",
    "        print(f\"   ✅ {file}\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"   ❌ {file}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣4️⃣ Example Prediction Function\n",
    "\n",
    "Here's how you would use your saved model to make predictions on new data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 14. QUICK PREDICTION EXAMPLE\n",
    "print(\"\\n1️⃣3️⃣ Example prediction function:\")\n",
    "print(\"\"\"\n",
    "def predict_stock_movement(latest_data_row):\n",
    "    '''Make prediction on new data'''\n",
    "    import joblib\n",
    "    model = joblib.load('models/stock_rf_model.pkl')  # or stock_lr_model.pkl\n",
    "    scaler = joblib.load('models/feature_scaler.pkl')\n",
    "    features = joblib.load('models/feature_columns.pkl')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Prepare data\n",
    "    X_latest = latest_data_row[features].fillna(method='ffill').fillna(method='bfill')\n",
    "    X_scaled = scaler.transform(X_latest)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Predict\n",
    "    prediction = model.predict(X_scaled)[0]\n",
    "    probability = model.predict_proba(X_scaled)[0][1]  # Probability of UP\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        'prediction': 'UP' if prediction == 1 else 'DOWN',\n",
    "        'probability_up': probability,\n",
    "        'confidence': max(probability, 1-probability)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
